The Recursive Remediation Trap — Named, Countered, and Made Structurally Impossible
Working title: Flow-Preserving Remediation Protocol (FPRP) + Flow Science Charter + The 2100 Visual Mandate

Mission: Eliminate the failure mode where every fix for a bottleneck reintroduces the same fatal weakness in the next turn, trapping the estate in a tail-chasing loop — and replace it with a protocol where flow is preserved by structured, time-bound loans that are repaid immediately and proven not to recur. Flow state becomes a first-class, measured, researched domain — and every visual is enforced at the 2100 alien standard by default, so the founder never has to ask again.

1. The peculiar failure mode — named
The Recursive Remediation Trap (RRT)
Every fix for a bottleneck either (a) reintroduces the exact class of weakness the guardrail existed to prevent, or (b) itself becomes the next bottleneck, or (c) trades one failure mode for its opposite — and each "fix" for the new symptom recreates the original problem. The estate oscillates forever, chasing its tail, never converging.

Sub-modes (all observed in IDP history)
Sub-mode	Pattern	Example
Guardrail bypass recursion	Fix requires bypassing a guardrail → bypass becomes permanent → guardrail decays → next incident → bypass again	Agent requests temporary permission, never returns it
Trade-off oscillation	Fix A creates B; fix B creates A; loop	Latency vs safety; speed vs review; autonomy vs control
Symptom migration	Fix hides the symptom; it reappears elsewhere	Patch the failing test; bug resurfaces in another test
Debt spiral	Quick fix adds debt; debt fix adds new debt; debt compounds	"Temporary" workarounds become permanent architecture
Authority creep	Fix requires more access; access is never clawed back; next fix requires more	The KLP violation, repeated
Standard erosion	Each fix lowers the bar slightly; bar never restored	"2100 standard" drifts to "whatever shipped"
Why this is existential for agentic systems
Agents loop faster than humans. A human tail-chases over weeks; an agent tail-chases over minutes. The trap compounds at machine speed.

Flow pressure rewards bypass. Agents optimise for the visible check, not the root cause.

Bypass is invisible unless tracked. The loan becomes permanent silently.

Without anti-recursion proof, the estate cannot distinguish a fix from a new instance of the disease.

This is the weakness the whole industry ignores. Naming it, tracking it, and making it structurally impossible is our asymmetric advantage.

